    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Poking at a level-premium cashflow\"\ndate: 2026-01-15\ncategories: [actuarial, python, interactive]\ndescription: \"A build-time, interactive Plotly view of expected cashflows for a simplified level-premium term policy.\"\nexecute:\n  echo: true\n  warning: false\n---\n\n```{=html}\n<button class=\"print-button no-print\" onclick=\"window.print()\" title=\"Print / Save as PDF\">\n  &#128424;&#65038; Print this post\n</button>\n```\n\n\nA toy but not-embarrassing projection: expected cashflows for a single-life,\nlevel-premium term policy. Everything runs **at build time** — the chart below is\nstatic Plotly HTML baked into the page, so there's no runtime and it stays on free\nstatic hosting. (When a reader actually needs to change inputs and re-run, that's\nwhen Quarto Live / Shinylive earn their weight — not here.)\n\nThe mortality basis is a Gompertz law, purely so the post is self-contained; swap\nin a real table when you want.\n\n::: {#d0ecc4aa .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nimport plotly.graph_objects as go\n\n# --- Assumptions -----------------------------------------------------------\nissue_age   = 45\nterm        = 20          # years\nsum_assured = 250_000\ni           = 0.04        # valuation rate\n# Gompertz mu(x) = B c^x, chosen to give sensible adult mortality\nB, c        = 3.0e-5, 1.09\n\n# --- Survival / mortality --------------------------------------------------\nages = issue_age + np.arange(term)\n# integrate mu over each policy year for a one-year death probability\ndef qx(age):\n    # ∫ B c^s ds from age to age+1  =  B (c^{age+1} - c^{age}) / ln c\n    Hx = B * (c**(age + 1) - c**age) / np.log(c)\n    return 1 - np.exp(-Hx)\n\nq = np.array([qx(a) for a in ages])\np = 1 - q\ntpx = np.concatenate(([1.0], np.cumprod(p)))[:term]   # prob in force at start of yr\n\n# --- Level net premium (equivalence principle) ----------------------------\nv = 1 / (1 + i)\ndisc_start = v ** np.arange(term)          # discount to start of each year\ndisc_end   = v ** (np.arange(term) + 1)\n\napv_benefits = np.sum(sum_assured * tpx * q * disc_end)      # death benefit APV\nannuity_due  = np.sum(tpx * disc_start)                      # ä for premiums\nnet_premium  = apv_benefits / annuity_due\n\n# --- Expected cashflows per year -------------------------------------------\nprem_in   = net_premium * tpx                 # collected while in force\nclaims_out = sum_assured * tpx * q            # expected death outgo\nnet_cf     = prem_in - claims_out\n\ndf = pd.DataFrame({\n    \"policy_year\": np.arange(1, term + 1),\n    \"premium_in\": prem_in,\n    \"claims_out\": claims_out,\n    \"net_cashflow\": net_cf,\n})\n```\n:::\n\n\nNet level premium comes out at **824** per year for a\n250\\,000 benefit.\n\n::: {#cell-fig-cashflow .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nfig = go.Figure()\nfig.add_bar(x=df.policy_year, y=df.premium_in,  name=\"Premium in\")\nfig.add_bar(x=df.policy_year, y=-df.claims_out, name=\"Claims out\")\nfig.add_scatter(x=df.policy_year, y=df.net_cashflow, name=\"Net cashflow\",\n                mode=\"lines+markers\", line=dict(width=3))\n\nfig.update_layout(\n    barmode=\"relative\",\n    template=\"plotly_white\",\n    xaxis_title=\"Policy year\",\n    yaxis_title=\"Expected cashflow\",\n    legend=dict(orientation=\"h\", y=1.12),\n    margin=dict(l=40, r=20, t=30, b=40),\n    height=430,\n)\nfig.show()\n```\n\n::: {#fig-cashflow .cell-output .cell-output-display}\n```{=html}\n<div>                            <div id=\"fddaaf4b-961b-492f-9aa2-501011ead764\" class=\"plotly-graph-div\" style=\"height:430px; width:100%;\"></div>            <script type=\"text/javascript\">                require([\"plotly\"], function(Plotly) {                    window.PLOTLYENV=window.PLOTLYENV || {};                                    if (document.getElementById(\"fddaaf4b-961b-492f-9aa2-501011ead764\")) {              